## 5.3 FortiGate Transit VLAN Interface

``` fortigate
config system interface
    edit "FW-TRANSIT"
        set vdom "root"
        set ip 10.255.100.2 255.255.255.252
        set allowaccess ping
        set device-identification enable
        set role lan
        set interface "internal"
        set vlanid 100
    next
end
```

### Explanation

-   Interface name: `FW-TRANSIT`
-   Parent interface: `internal`
-   VLAN ID: `100`
-   IP address: `10.255.100.2/30`
-   The interface is used as the routed transit point toward the Core
    Switch.

This is a VLAN subinterface. The FortiGate receives VLAN 100 traffic
over the trunk connected to the parent interface.

