## 5.4 FortiGate Static Routes

The FortiGate must know how to reach the internal VLAN networks through
the Core Switch.

``` fortigate
config router static
    edit 0
        set dst 192.168.1.0 255.255.255.0
        set gateway 10.255.100.1 !gateway is the SVI vlan100 in coreswitch
        set device "FW-TRANSIT"
    next
    edit 0
        set dst 192.168.2.0 255.255.255.0
        set gateway 10.255.100.1
        set device "FW-TRANSIT"
    next
    edit 0
        set dst 192.168.3.0 255.255.255.0
        set gateway 10.255.100.1
        set device "FW-TRANSIT"
    next
    edit 0
        set dst 192.168.4.0 255.255.255.0
        set gateway 10.255.100.1
        set device "FW-TRANSIT"
    next
end
```

### Route Purpose

  Destination      Next Hop       Interface
  ---------------- -------------- ------------
  192.168.1.0/24   10.255.100.1   FW-TRANSIT
  192.168.2.0/24   10.255.100.1   FW-TRANSIT
  192.168.3.0/24   10.255.100.1   FW-TRANSIT
  192.168.4.0/24   10.255.100.1   FW-TRANSIT

> Check the existing routing table before adding duplicate routes. The
> FortiGate also needs a valid default route toward the ISP.

