## 6.6 Core-to-FortiGate Trunk

Current configuration:

``` cisco
interface TenGigabitEthernet1/0/7
 description TRUNK-TO-FORTIGATE
 switchport trunk native vlan 999
 switchport trunk allowed vlan 100
 switchport mode trunk
```

### Explanation

-   The port operates as an 802.1Q trunk.
-   VLAN 100 is allowed on the trunk.
-   VLAN 999 is configured as the native VLAN.
-   The FortiGate transit interface uses VLAN ID 100.

### Native VLAN 999

Create the VLAN if it does not already exist:

``` cisco
vlan 999
 name UNUSED-NATIVE
exit
```

No SVI or DHCP pool is required for VLAN 999 in this design.

> The native VLAN must be deliberately configured and matched as
> required by the trunk design. Do not assume that a native VLAN is
> automatically a security control by itself.

