## 7.5 L2 Access Switch Trunk Uplink

Current configuration:

``` cisco
interface GigabitEthernet1/1/4
 description TRUNK-Switch100
 switchport trunk native vlan 100
 switchport trunk allowed vlan 10-40,100
 switchport mode trunk
```

### Explanation

This trunk carries:

-   VLAN 10
-   VLAN 20
-   VLAN 30
-   VLAN 40
-   VLAN 100

The native VLAN is 100 on this uplink according to the provided
configuration.

> The Core-to-Access trunk and Core-to-FortiGate trunk use different
> native VLAN settings in the supplied configuration. Document them
> separately and ensure each link's two endpoints agree on the intended
> native VLAN behavior.

