# 11. Key Learning Points

## VLAN

A VLAN logically separates Layer 2 networks.

## SVI

An SVI provides a Layer 3 interface for a VLAN. In this lab, the Core
Switch SVI is the default gateway for each client VLAN.

## Trunk

A trunk carries traffic for multiple VLANs between network devices.

## Native VLAN

The native VLAN is used for untagged traffic on an 802.1Q trunk. The two
endpoints must be designed and configured consistently.

## Static Routing

Static routing manually defines the next hop or path to a destination
network.

## Default Route

A default route is used when no more specific route exists.

## DHCP

DHCP automatically provides client IP configuration, including:

-   IP address
-   Subnet mask
-   Default gateway
-   DNS server

## Firewall Policy

A FortiGate firewall policy controls whether traffic is allowed between
interfaces and can apply NAT and security processing.

