## 16. Final Architecture Summary

The Cisco L3 Core Switch acts as the internal routing and DHCP device.
The FortiGate-80F acts as the security gateway toward the Internet. VLAN
100 provides the transit connection between the two devices, while VLANs
10, 20, 30, and 40 provide separate internal networks for the different
departments.

The architecture uses static routing between the Core Switch and
FortiGate rather than OSPF.

